  "notes": [
    "Canonical values are monthly. Convenience input shelter_costs is treated as total shelter costs for this Axiom case.",
    "Utility allowance outputs are requested separately so client parity tools can identify whether another engine adds them by default.",
    "The Colorado corpus-direct composition rounds the excess shelter deduction to whole dollars (floor(x + 0.5) in us:regulations/7-cfr/273/10#snap_excess_shelter_cost as composed for Colorado): excess shelter is 525 and net income 226. PolicyEngine keeps cents (524.5 / 226.5), so the external comparison shows a fifty-cent net-income delta by design; the rounding question is tracked in rulespec-us#1167."
  ],
